            <ArticleTitle>[Analgesia by electric current in the early postoperative period].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>125-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In 295 patients in the early postoperative period anesthesia was performed by means of percutaneous electrostimulation with a new national apparatus Eliman-101. The authors note high efficiency of such analgesia in 63,4% of the patients, satisfactory results were obtained in 32,3%. No sufficient anesthesia was achieved in 13 patients (4,3%). There were no side effects and complications.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
